# No em dash

Do not use an em dash (U+2014) in user-facing text (UI copy, code strings shown to users) or in code comments. Documentation (Markdown files) is exempt (owner decision, 2026-10-07).

End the sentence, or rewrite the line. When a dash is still needed, use a hyphen with spaces: ` - `.

Empty placeholders use `-`.

Checked by `tests/noEmdash.test.js` in every repo's `npm test` (CI included): it scans the code (Go, JS, Svelte, CSS, HTML, shell, SQL, workflow YAML) and skips Markdown, `docs/` and data.
